               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female admitted on 05/08/2022 with acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray was performed, excluding pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Spirometry supported obstructive ventilatory pattern consistent with known COPD. Treatment consisted of inhaled short-acting bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy with satisfactory clinical response. The patient was discharged on 06/08/2022 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of her regular inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
